<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L2_2_3" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-02">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L2_2_3">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L2_2_3" name="2.3 Mine Services (L2)" processRef="Process_L2_2_3"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L2_2_3" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L2 Process Area. Ancillary physical operations that maintain conditions necessary for productive extraction and hauling: haul road maintenance, pit dewatering, and slope stability monitoring. Do not directly move ore but their failure halts operations that do.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L2_2_3">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L2_2_3_rm" name="Road Maintenance Operator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L2_2_3_s1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Xsub_L2_2_3_g1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L2_2_3_e1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L2_2_3_dw" name="Dewatering Operator / SCADA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L2_2_3_s2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Xsub_L2_2_3_g2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L2_2_3_e2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L2_2_3_gt" name="Geotechnical Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L2_2_3_s3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Xsub_L2_2_3_g3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L2_2_3_e3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L2_2_3_s1" name="Shift start or road condition call">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g1" name="2.3.1 Haul Road Maintenance">
      <bpmn:documentation>L0/L2 Process. Haul road condition directly affects truck speed, tyre life, and fuel consumption. Grading and dust suppression are the two primary maintenance activities.
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Road Maintenance Operator; Services Supervisor
Standard alignment: GMG TUM; ISA-95 Level 0
DDVC layer: Raw</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_1" name="2.3.1.1 Grade Haul Road Surface">
        <bpmn:documentation>Motor grader operator systematically grades haul road segments to remove ruts, loose material, and corrugation, restoring a smooth, correctly cambered running surface. Grader performing road maintenance is classified WT per GMG TUM. Road segment graded, operator, and duration are the key data outputs.
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: Road Maintenance Operator
Standard alignment: GMG TUM (WT for grader — primary function); GMG Mobile Equipment Open Data
DDVC layer: Raw</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_in_2_3_1_2</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:task>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_2" name="2.3.1.2 Apply Dust Suppression">
        <bpmn:documentation>Water truck operator applies water to haul road surfaces to suppress dust generated by truck traffic, improving visibility and reducing airborne particulate matter. Water truck performing dust suppression is classified WT per GMG TUM. Volume of water applied per road segment is a reportable environmental data point in some jurisdictions.
ISA-95 level: 0 / 2
Actors: Road Maintenance Operator
Standard alignment: GMG TUM (WT for water truck — primary function)
DDVC layer: Raw</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_in_2_3_1_2</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:task>
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_in_2_3_1_2" sourceRef="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_1" targetRef="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_2"/>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L2_2_3_e1" name="Road maintenance records submitted">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_2</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L2_2_3_s2" name="Sump level above setpoint">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g2" name="2.3.2 Pit Dewatering">
      <bpmn:documentation>L0/L1/L2 Process. Accumulates water is pumped from the active pit to surface via submersible sump pumps and dewatering bores. Failure to dewater effectively results in bench instability, haul road damage, and blast design constraint.
ISA-95 level: 0–2
Actors: Dewatering Operator; Mine Services Supervisor
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 0–2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: dewatering_pump_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_1" name="2.3.2.1 Operate Sump Pump">
        <bpmn:documentation>Submersible pump(s) continuously or intermittently pump accumulated water from the pit sump to a surface discharge point. Operation is automated via level switch or SCADA control, with manual override. Pump telemetry (flow rate, discharge pressure, motor current, run hours) is logged to PI Historian. Sump water level measured by float switch or ultrasonic level sensor.
ISA-95 level: 1 / 0
Actors: Dewatering Operator; Automated SCADA
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: dewatering_pump_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:task>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_2" name="2.3.2.2 Operate Dewatering Bore">
        <bpmn:documentation>Vertical dewatering bores pump groundwater from the aquifer layer, reducing pore water pressure in pit walls and improving slope stability. Bore pump operation typically automated. Bore pump telemetry logged to PI Historian. Bore water chemistry may be sampled periodically for regulatory compliance.
ISA-95 level: 1 / 0
Actors: Dewatering Operator; Automated SCADA
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: dewatering_pump_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:task>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L2_2_3_e2" name="Water pumped to surface">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L2_2_3_s3" name="Scan interval or alert trigger">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:subProcess id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g3" name="2.3.3 Slope Stability Monitoring">
      <bpmn:documentation>L1/L2/L3 Process. Geotechnical instrumentation continuously monitors pit wall displacement and pore water pressure to detect precursor signs of slope instability. Safety-critical monitoring function. Displacement alerts can trigger exclusion zones and production interruptions classified as TUM delays.
ISA-95 level: 1–3
Actors: Geotechnical Engineer; Mine Controller
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1–3; GMG TUM (displacement alert → production delay classification)
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: slope_monitoring_telemetry); Curated (slope_monitoring_reading)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L2_2_3_6</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_1" name="2.3.3.1 Collect Prism and Radar Displacement Data">
        <bpmn:documentation>Robotic total station surveys retroreflective prisms installed on pit walls at regular intervals (typically 15–60 min), computing 3D displacement vectors for each prism. Ground-based slope monitoring radar (GBSAR) provides continuous surface displacement maps, updated at 15–60 minute scan intervals. Both datasets are time-stamped in UTC. Velocity thresholds trigger automated alerts.
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: Geotechnical Engineer; Automated monitoring system
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 1 (sensing); ISA-95 Level 2 (monitoring/alert)
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: slope_monitoring_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:task>
      <bpmn:task id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_2" name="2.3.3.2 Read and Assess Piezometer Data">
        <bpmn:documentation>Vibrating wire piezometers in geotechnical boreholes measure pore water pressure at specific depth horizons. Data loggers record pressure readings at 15–60 min intervals and transmit via telemetry to the geotechnical database. Geotechnical engineer reviews trends for rising pore pressure anomalies. Anomalous readings trigger engineering assessment and potential dewatering response or operational constraint.
ISA-95 level: 1 / 3
Actors: Geotechnical Engineer
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 3
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series); Curated (geotechnical_reading)</bpmn:documentation>
      </bpmn:task>
    </bpmn:subProcess>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L2_2_3_e3" name="Readings recorded; alerts routed">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L2_2_3_6</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_1" sourceRef="Start_L2_2_3_s1" targetRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_2" sourceRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g1" targetRef="End_L2_2_3_e1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_3" sourceRef="Start_L2_2_3_s2" targetRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_4" sourceRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g2" targetRef="End_L2_2_3_e2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_5" sourceRef="Start_L2_2_3_s3" targetRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L2_2_3_6" sourceRef="Xsub_L2_2_3_g3" targetRef="End_L2_2_3_e3"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L2_2_3">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L2_2_3" bpmnElement="Collab_L2_2_3">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L2_2_3_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L2_2_3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="722" height="868"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L2_2_3_rm_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L2_2_3_rm" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="682" height="212"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L2_2_3_dw_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L2_2_3_dw" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="232" width="682" height="328"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L2_2_3_gt_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L2_2_3_gt" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="560" width="682" height="328"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L2_2_3_s1_di" bpmnElement="Start_L2_2_3_s1"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="98" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="160" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g1_di" bpmnElement="Xsub_L2_2_3_g1" isExpanded="true"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="50" width="424" height="152"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_1"><dc:Bounds x="226" y="98" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_1_2"><dc:Bounds x="432" y="98" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_in_2_3_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_in_2_3_1_2"><di:waypoint x="396" y="138"/><di:waypoint x="432" y="138"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L2_2_3_e1_di" bpmnElement="End_L2_2_3_e1"><dc:Bounds x="662" y="98" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="640" y="160" width="100" height="56"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L2_2_3_s2_di" bpmnElement="Start_L2_2_3_s2"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="368" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="430" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g2_di" bpmnElement="Xsub_L2_2_3_g2" isExpanded="true"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="262" width="424" height="268"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_1"><dc:Bounds x="329" y="310" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_2_2"><dc:Bounds x="329" y="426" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L2_2_3_e2_di" bpmnElement="End_L2_2_3_e2"><dc:Bounds x="662" y="368" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="640" y="430" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L2_2_3_s3_di" bpmnElement="Start_L2_2_3_s3"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="696" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="758" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Xsub_L2_2_3_g3_di" bpmnElement="Xsub_L2_2_3_g3" isExpanded="true"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="590" width="424" height="268"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_1"><dc:Bounds x="329" y="638" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L2_2_3_2_3_3_2"><dc:Bounds x="329" y="754" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L2_2_3_e3_di" bpmnElement="End_L2_2_3_e3"><dc:Bounds x="662" y="696" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="640" y="758" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_1"><di:waypoint x="166" y="126"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="126"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_2"><di:waypoint x="626" y="126"/><di:waypoint x="662" y="126"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_3"><di:waypoint x="166" y="396"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="396"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_4"><di:waypoint x="626" y="396"/><di:waypoint x="662" y="396"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_5"><di:waypoint x="166" y="724"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="724"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L2_2_3_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L2_2_3_6"><di:waypoint x="626" y="724"/><di:waypoint x="662" y="724"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
